{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0164","billNumberShort":"H.B. 164","billNumberLong":"HB0164S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0023","shortTitle":"Health Care Patient Reporting to the Division of Professional Licensing","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"GRICIS","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Gricius, Stephanie","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"PITCHS","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Pitcher, Stephanie","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses nondisclosure clauses and required disclosures that must be made to a patient regarding reporting to the Division of Professional Licensing.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>requires health care providers that receive a disclosure of potential unprofessional or unlawful conduct to provide information about how to report the concern to the Division of Professional Licensing;<hr><ltbullet>makes the validity of a nondisclosure clause preventing a patient from reporting the conduct of the patient's health care provider to the Division of Professional Licensing contingent on the provider having provided the division's model notice to the patient before the execution of the nondisclosure clause;<hr><ltbullet>requires the division to make a model notice and publish the notice online for download; and<hr><ltbullet>defines terms.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Kami Orton","fiscalAnalyst":"Sean C. Faherty","lastAction":"Governor Vetoed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/26/2026","trackingID":"QNXTHPVSGS","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-07 10:42:56.227","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","a